# rule.always.itemize-the-fulcrums-you-best-guess

when you best-guess a fork mid-drive, itemize it **at that moment**; never at the end, never only in yield prose.

```
$route/.fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums._.md               # SUMMARY
$route/.fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F$n-$slug.md  # one ENTRY per fulcrum
```

both owed. append at the moment, never in a sweep. a call under 93% confidence is a trigger too, even with no alternative weighed (n=1 generalization, unfetched premise, invented taxonomy, an act against a stated bound, "i think this is right").

summary columns: `case` · `title` · `rework` (clean/dirty) · `status` · `confidence` (a percentage). entry adds: the fork stated fairly · taken, why · rework, why · confidence, why low · where · verdict once ruled.

blocker: a fulcrum never itemized · row with no entry or entry with no row · record swept at the end · absent `rework` column · prose filename · unrecorded verdict · sub-93% call with no row · percentage with no reason.
